<!--
  SYNTHETIC, NON-CUI ORACLE PROBE. Hand-authored MSPDI (MS Project XML).
  Fictional content; contains no real schedule data of any kind.

  PURPOSE — settle ONE open question with ONE Acumen Fuse run.
  ADR-0280 ASSUMES Acumen Fuse compares Total Float in WHOLE DAYS, so a sub-day
  negative float (e.g. -0.25 d) reads as 0 and is NOT counted by DCMA "7. Negative
  Float". The NASA .aft metric library carries NO <Formula> for that metric (prose
  only: "Activities that are incomplete and have total float less than 0 working
  days"), so the assumption cannot be checked against a formula — only empirically.
  This file puts sub-day AND whole-day negative float in the same schedule, with
  controls, so a single Fuse run tells us which rows Fuse counts.

  HOW TO READ IT — every activity's NAME states its intended Total Float.

    UID 101  NEG-SUBDAY-025   TF = -0.25 d (-120 min)  DISCRIMINATOR
    UID 102  NEG-SUBDAY-050   TF = -0.50 d (-240 min)  DISCRIMINATOR (rounding tie)
    UID 103  NEG-SUBDAY-075   TF = -0.75 d (-360 min)  DISCRIMINATOR (round vs truncate)
    UID 104  NEG-WHOLEDAY-1   TF = -1.00 d (-480 min)  CONTROL - must be counted
    UID 105  NEG-WHOLEDAY-2   TF = -2.00 d (-960 min)  CONTROL - must be counted
    UID 106  ZERO-FLOAT       TF =  0.00 d (   0 min)  CONTROL - must NOT be counted
    UID 107  POSITIVE-FLOAT   TF = +8.00 d (+3840 min) CONTROL - must NOT be counted
    UID 108  PROJECT-DRIVER   TF =  0.00 d (   0 min)  sets the project finish (46 d long)
    UID 109  HIGH-WHOLEDAY-45 TF = +45.00 d (21600 min) CONTROL - must be counted by 6. High Float
    UID 110  HIGH-SUBDAY-4475 TF = +44.75 d (21480 min) DISCRIMINATOR (round vs truncate)
    UID 111  HIGH-SUBDAY-4450 TF = +44.50 d (21360 min) DISCRIMINATOR (rounding tie)
    UID 112  HIGH-SUBDAY-4425 TF = +44.25 d (21240 min) DISCRIMINATOR (any whole-day rule drops it)
    UID 113  HIGH-WHOLEDAY-44 TF = +44.00 d (21120 min) CONTROL - must NOT be counted (not > 44)

  STATUS AFTER ADR-0514 (R-03, 2026-09-20): the FIELD's rule is now KNOWN from the operator's
  own Fuse exports — the Total Float Fuse displays beside every activity of the Large Test File
  pair is the stored slack rounded HALF-TO-EVEN to whole days (196 exact half-day floats,
  513.5 -> 514 and 514.5 -> 514), and the "6. High Float" / "7. Negative Float" sets are
  UID-exact against the engine under that field on both snapshots. What this run still settles
  DIRECTLY is the filter's reading at the two ties themselves (-0.50 d and +44.50 d), which no
  corpus activity occupies: expected under the measured rule, 102 NOT counted by 7. Negative
  Float and 111 NOT counted by 6. High Float. The run is a confirmation, not a blocker.

  If Fuse's Negative Float detail does NOT list 104 and 105, or its High Float 44d detail
  does NOT list 109, the run is broken or misconfigured and proves nothing — check that
  first, before reading 101/102/103 and 110/111/112.

  DESIGN NOTES (why it is built this way — do not "tidy" these away):
  * NO logic links, by design. Every activity is independent, so each row's total
    float is authored solely by its own Finish-No-Later-Than constraint and nothing
    propagates between rows; the positive floats are authored by the 46-day PROJECT-DRIVER
    (float = project finish - own finish) and the +8 d control by its own constraint.
    (Cost: DCMA "1. Logic" will read 100% on this file. Ignore every check except
    7. Negative Float and 6. High Float.)
  * EVERY task carries Baseline Number 0 with Duration > 0 whole working days. The
    .aft's "7. Negative Float" PrimaryFilter is literally
    [Baseline Duration GreaterThan 0] AND [Total Float LessThan 0]; a task without a
    baseline duration falls silently OUT of the measured population.
  * All tasks are 0% complete (Planned). The .aft filter is
    IncludePlanned=true, IncludeInProgress=true, IncludeComplete=FALSE.
  * The working day is ONE contiguous 8-hour block, 08:00-16:00, with NO lunch break,
    so the engine's single-block day model and MS Project's calendar agree on intraday
    arithmetic exactly (a 08:00-12:00 / 13:00-17:00 calendar makes every afternoon
    instant differ by 60 min between the two models - fatal for a sub-day probe).
  * Belt and braces: every constraint instant is in the MORNING (10:00 / 12:00) and
    every activity finish is either a morning instant or an end-of-day boundary, so
    the intended floats survive even if MS Project substitutes a classic
    08:00-12:00 / 13:00-17:00 calendar on import.
-->
